  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-VNM901</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National institutions and systems are enhanced for the promotion, development, and implementation of the integrated policy for social justice through decent work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam has demonstrated commitment to renovate and improve the quality of social policies in line with the Global Accelerator on Jobs and Social Protection for Just Transitions. Recently, Viet Nam released its political declaration on the Just Energy Transition Partnership (JETP). The cross-cutting nature of the JETP is critically important, including social policy, social protection, nature, and health, among others.  The JETP and the new resolution mentioned above emphasize the importance of social investments to improve decent work opportunities and social protection, especially for disadvantaged and vulnerable groups.The country&#x2019;s Socio-Economic Development Strategy 2021-2030 recognizes informality as a hindrance to inclusive growth. 
In collaboration with tripartite constituents, ILO supports Viet Nam&#x2019;s efforts to advance social justice and strengthen the social dimension of sustainable development. It addresses key barriers such as inequality, informality, limited social protection, and lack of decent work&#x2014;particularly affecting vulnerable and rural populations. The programme promotes inclusive policies, institutional capacity-building, and pathways for a just transition.
In addition, typhoon Yagi, which struck in September 2024, severely impacted many provinces in Viet Nam, resulting in significant loss of life and disruption to livelihoods, infrastructure, and employment. In response, the ILO partnered with national and local stakeholders to provide timely support for early recovery, focusing on employment and livelihood restoration.</narrative>
  </description>
